   $q$Why is the ridership of the old ferry less relevant than the author suggests?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The ferry ran when there was no bridge, so riders then had no faster choice.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Wrenfield's ferry carries fewer riders, so the two numbers contradict each other.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-comparison"},{"text":"The figure of six hundred riders is too small to matter for a town this size.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The author does not say what the ferry tickets cost in those years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The ferry ran when there was no bridge, so riders then had no faster choice.$q$, $q$The passage says the ferry ran "until 1961, when the bridge opened," so its riders had no bridge to drive across; that tells little about demand now. Ticket prices might be interesting, but they are not the main reason the old figure fails to fit today's situation.$q$, 'draft', '32b79aa6-b1ec-585c-ac90-c70bc121520d')
