   $q$Which discovery would most weaken Szabo's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Proof that the ledgers greatly undercounted cargo during the 1860s.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A diary describing how hard the 1871 drought was on canal families.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"consistent-with-claim"},{"text":"Records showing the railroad carried more freight each year after 1858.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-reasoning"},{"text":"More letters from merchants praising the speed of the railroad.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-reasoning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Proof that the ledgers greatly undercounted cargo during the 1860s.$q$, $q$Szabo's case "begins with the canal company's own ledgers," so if they undercounted 1860s cargo, the early decline might not be real. A diary about families' hardship fits her view, since she says the drought mattered to them.$q$, 'draft', 'b116a008-5aaa-5731-ac44-593527db3f0b')
