   $q$Why are the volunteers' water tests relevant to the author's claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They prove that geese prefer the picnic areas to quieter spots.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They explain why goslings at the pond developed weak wing bones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"They link areas of heavy feeding to more nutrients and algae in the water.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They show that bread is low in protein and minerals.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They link areas of heavy feeding to more nutrients and algae in the water.$q$, $q$The tests found "higher nutrient levels and thicker green algae" near the heavy feeding areas, which supports the point that rotting bread harms the water. The protein point concerns the birds' diet, a different reason.$q$, 'draft', '4347f33f-951e-5cbd-95ac-5e1953240d65')
