  ('ae152a16-d9a9-535d-b14f-3b4352e6bae2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence makes a claim that the author does not support with evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each summer, our volunteer group tests the water at six spots.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepts-supported-claim"},{"text":"Young birds that eat mostly bread can develop weak wing bones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepts-supported-claim"},{"text":"With so many birds crowded together, they must be getting sick more often.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The number of geese has also climbed, from about 40 to more than 200.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepts-supported-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With so many birds crowded together, they must be getting sick more often.$q$, $q$The author offers no illness records for the flock; "must be getting sick" is an assumption. The goose count is a reported observation, and the claim about weak wing bones is backed by the county wildlife office's records of goslings at Millbrook.$q$, 'draft', '4347f33f-951e-5cbd-95ac-5e1953240d65')
