  ('d7430866-8c3b-58fd-be9a-2e5d1ccff8a5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-argument-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$What is the main problem with the author's reasoning that bread "is clearly to blame" for the rise in geese?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author admits that geese do not eat bread at Millbrook Pond.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The goose count covers too long a period to be meaningful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The author shows the numbers rose but gives no evidence that bread caused it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author's water tests show that bread does not affect the pond.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author shows the numbers rose but gives no evidence that bread caused it.$q$, $q$A rising goose count alone does not show why the birds came; other causes are never considered or ruled out, so the causal claim goes beyond the evidence. Five years is a reasonable period, so the length of time is not the flaw.$q$, 'draft', '4347f33f-951e-5cbd-95ac-5e1953240d65')
